  "editorial_note": "GitHub listed fifteen projects this Sunday morning, and nine of them were featured here in the past week, so they stay out. Today's five picks are all first appearances: the ==token-cutting layer for coding agents== Caveman, Tencent's ==self-hosted workflow engine for coding agents== LoopForge, the Univer spreadsheet and document SDK, the AG-UI protocol for putting agents into apps, and the Linux Wi-Fi auditing tool Airgorah. Curation order reflects practical interest, not GitHub rank. Trending is not a release date or an endorsement.",
  "coverage_notes": [
    "GitHub's daily listing held 15 rows at capture. The capture parsed exactly fifteen listing rows and is GitHub's own list, not a truncation by us.",
    "All 15 listing entries were inspected. Exact public GitHub API metadata and README files of the six new candidates were read between 07:01:04 and 07:01:10 UTC, and recent releases at about 07:01:30 UTC. Every checked repository was active and unarchived.",
    "Nine entries featured in the past seven days were left out: we-promise/sure (11 November), GoogleChrome/modern-web-guidance-src (12 November), QwenLM/qwen-code and ashhart/TensorFold (13 November), and backnotprop/plannotator, tradermonty/claude-trading-skills, ChromeDevTools/chrome-devtools-mcp, alibaba/open-code-review and louislam/uptime-kuma (14 November). Their newest releases since those picks are patch, nightly or alpha builds, which we did not judge a material change.",
    "Likely7/Veyra-NRVideo (GPL-3.0, Windows video enhancement) was again not picked: its listing line promises '120FPS with DLSS 5' for a console game, a marketing claim we could not verify from primary sources.",
    "Tencent/LoopForge shows NOASSERTION in GitHub's license detection; its LICENSE file was read directly and states MIT for LoopForge, with bundled third-party components under their own licenses.",
    "The preceding seven calendar dates, 8-14 November, were checked for local history; all seven editions exist.",
    "The official listing was captured at 08:00:48 Europe/Paris. Literal stars-today labels are GitHub's displayed period figures; API total stars and README evidence were checked separately at the times shown per card. They are not an independently audited rolling 24-hour growth measurement.",
    "Feature descriptions, benchmark, adoption and performance figures come from each project's own README and release notes and are the maintainers' claims. No candidate code, installer, CLI, app, skill or model was installed, downloaded or run, and none of this is a security audit or endorsement."
  ],
