    {
      "repository": "JuliusBrussee/caveman",
      "url": "https://github.com/JuliusBrussee/caveman",
      "trending_rank": 10,
      "description": "A token-saving layer for AI coding agents: a skill makes the agent answer in terse caveman style, and a local proxy shrinks logs, JSON and test output before the model reads them, for Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, OpenCode and other agents.",
      "why_interesting": "It attacks agent cost from both ends, ==shorter answers and smaller inputs==, while keeping code exact. The README is unusually candid about its numbers, linking a page of cases where it loses and noting that an interim Auto benchmark is half done; its savings figures, such as 33.2% fewer input tokens per session, are maintainer measurements.",
      "caveat": "The CLI ==sends usage statistics by default==, including a random install ID, OS and IP, until telemetry is turned off, and the optional Auto router sends your latest prompts and attached files to Caveman Cloud. The installer finds and changes the configuration of agents already on your machine.",
      "category": "AI agents / developer tools",
      "language": "Go",
      "license": "Apache-2.0",
      "stars_total": 120183,
      "stars_period": 227,
