    {
      "repository": "Tencent/LoopForge",
      "url": "https://github.com/Tencent/LoopForge",
      "trending_rank": 13,
      "description": "A self-hosted workspace from Tencent for shipping software with coding agents: a chat bot opens Docker sandboxes with your repositories and opens pull requests, and proven ways of working are saved as SOPs that chain agent, script and human-approval steps.",
      "why_interesting": "It treats agents as ==a repeatable delivery pipeline with human gates== rather than one-off chats: planning, implementation, review and testing get separate roles, and every change links back to a tracked requirement. It drives ten existing agent CLIs, including Codex, Claude Code and OpenCode, instead of shipping its own model.",
      "caveat": "It is ==early software, at version 0.3.x== with release candidates still appearing, and runs as a Docker stack with MySQL. Several internal features, such as requirement clarification and bot replies, currently use Tencent's CodeBuddy only, and each executor needs its own paid model credentials.",
      "category": "AI agents / software delivery",
      "language": "Go",
      "license": "MIT",
