    {
      "repository": "ag-ui-protocol/ag-ui",
      "url": "https://github.com/ag-ui-protocol/ag-ui",
      "trending_rank": 8,
      "description": "AG-UI is an open, event-based protocol for connecting AI agents to user-facing applications: agent backends emit a small set of standard events for streaming chat, shared state, tool calls and human approval, over any transport.",
      "why_interesting": "It fills ==the agent-to-interface gap that MCP and A2A leave open==, so a frontend can talk to agents built on different frameworks the same way. The README lists integrations for LangGraph, CrewAI, Google ADK, Microsoft Agent Framework and the Claude Agent SDK, plus client SDKs in several languages.",
      "caveat": "It is ==driven mainly by CopilotKit==, and many integration docs point to CopilotKit's own site; several language SDKs are marked community-maintained. A protocol is only as useful as its adoption, and the OpenAI Agents SDK integration is still listed as in progress.",
      "category": "AI agents / protocol",
